Fixed several bugs when running on macOS:

- TCP SYN online checks treated "connection refused" as offline on macOS, so hosts with closed ports were reported as down.
- MAC address lookups failed and logged an error for every host, since macOS has no ``/proc/net/arp``. The ARP cache is now read with ``arp -an``.
- Raw packet capability is now detected by opening a BPF device, which is what Scapy uses on macOS, and PEAT suggests ``sudo`` when it isn't available.
- Promiscuous mode detection now works on macOS.
- Serial ports given as paths containing dashes (e.g. ``/dev/cu.usbserial-1410`` or ``/dev/serial/by-id/...``) were rejected. On macOS, numeric serial port values now refer to the sorted ``/dev/cu.*`` devices.
- The default interface MAC address was set to the interface's IP address.
